1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,404
Your processor says 4 gigahertz.

2
00:00:02,684 --> 00:00:04,341
What is it actually counting?

3
00:00:05,091 --> 00:00:09,030
Inside the CPU is a clock that ticks, like a metronome.

4
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:13,053
Every tick, the processor can move its work one step forward.

5
00:00:13,803 --> 00:00:16,478
Gigahertz means billions of ticks per second.

6
00:00:16,758 --> 00:00:20,806
So 4 gigahertz is four billion ticks, every single second.

7
00:00:21,556 --> 00:00:24,704
But a higher number doesn't always mean a faster chip.

8
00:00:24,984 --> 00:00:32,350
Newer processors get more work done on every tick, so a newer chip at 4 gigahertz can beat an older one at 5.

9
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:37,148
Clock speed is how fast it ticks, not how much it does each tick.

10
00:00:37,428 --> 00:00:39,994
More PC hardware explained on the channel.

